Article 3 A circuit court shall try or handle the following cases within the circuit area that shall be accepted by the Supreme People's Court:
(1) First-instance administrative cases that are major and complex nationwide;
(2) First-instance civil and commercial cases that have significant impact nationwide;
(3) Cases appealed against first-instance administrative or civil/commercial judgments or rulings rendered by a Higher People's Court;
(4) Applications for retrial against administrative or civil/commercial judgments, rulings, or mediation statements that have become legally effective and were rendered by a Higher People's Court;
(5) Criminal petition cases;
(6) Cases handled by initiating a retrial ex officio according to law;
(7) Cases of application for reconsideration against decisions on fines or detention rendered by a Higher People's Court;
(8) Cases submitted by a Higher People's Court to the Supreme People's Court for a ruling or decision due to jurisdictional issues;
(9) Cases submitted by a Higher People's Court for approval of extension of the trial period;
(10) Civil and commercial cases involving Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, and judicial assistance cases;
(11) Other cases that the Supreme People's Court considers shall be tried or handled by a circuit court.
The circuit court shall, according to law, handle letters and visits addressed to the Supreme People's Court within the circuit area.
